# Model economy

Motto: **min tokens → max measured result.** A large model is a scarce tool, not the default worker.

## 1. Tier the work (before you act)

| Tier | Use | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Script / tools** | No LLM | `gate.sh`, pytest, `rg`, `cmp`, SHA, link check, regenerate CARD |
| **Cheap model** | Mechanical, bounded, low judgment | grep/explore, boilerplate, format edits, commit message draft, golden-file refresh, STATUS log lines |
| **Large model** | Hard judgment only | licence/ADR, architecture fork, audit of claims, multi-repo trade-offs, novel failure diagnosis |

If the step is tier-Script, **do not** ask a model. If tier-Cheap, **do not** keep a frontier model on it.

## 2. When YOU are the large model

- One focus from `STATUS.md` §Next — no side quests.
- Prefer `rg` / targeted `Read` over dumping whole trees into context.
- Do not re-read files you already have this turn.
- Cap Session-log / ADR / commit prose; no essay when a table works.
- Do not spawn parallel subagents for work one agent finishes in <15 min.
- Stop and ask the human before a second expensive wave.

## 3. Subagents — pick the cheap slot

When launching `Task` / subagents, set `model` explicitly:

- **Default for explore / shell / mechanical briefs:** `composer-2.5-fast` or `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast`
- **Inherit / frontier only when** the brief needs architecture judgment, licence/legal reading, or cross-doc conflict resolution
- Never give five frontier agents the same repo tour — one explore pass, then disjoint file ownership

Brief = DoD + owned paths + “do not git”. Not a second copy of AGENTS.md.

## 4. Switch signal (tell the human)

Ask to continue in a cheaper chat / model when the remaining work is:

- doc typo / STATUS log / rename / golden refresh
- “run the gate and paste PASS”
- mechanical apply of an already-decided patch

Phrase: *«Дальше механическое — лучше дешёвая модель / Composer.»*

## 5. Anti-patterns (token burn)

- Full-repo audits “just in case”
- Parallel agents with overlapping file ownership
- Pasting large tool outputs back into the prompt when a path + line range suffices
- Re-deriving facts already in `STATUS.md` / `CLAIMS.md` / ADR
- Long self-summaries of work the human can see in `git log`
